---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
// Keep this page in step with what the site actually runs: the contact
// form (Formspree), Vercel hosting and Web Analytics, and Google Fonts.
// Update the date whenever the substance changes.
const updated = 'October 17, 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="How brandonfreitag.com handles what you share through its contact form, and what the site records about visits.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <h2>The contact form</h2>
  <p>The site collects personal information only when you send a message through the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>: your name, your email address, and what you write. Formspree, the form service, delivers the message to Brandon by email and keeps a copy of the submission. It is used only to reply to you, and it is not sold or shared with anyone else. To have a message deleted, say so through the same form.</p>

  <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
  <p>The site counts visits with Vercel Web Analytics, which records the pages viewed, the referring site, and general device and country information. It uses no cookies and does not identify you or follow you across other sites.</p>

  <h2>Hosting, fonts, and cookies</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted by Vercel, which keeps standard server logs, including IP addresses, for security and operations. Its fonts load from Google Fonts, so your browser's request for them reaches Google. The site sets no cookies and runs no advertising or tracking beyond what is described here.</p>
</Base>

<style>
  .updated {
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
</style>
